WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.830
What will happen if Joe Biden defeats Donald
Trump in November?

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:10.759
And then you get a two and a half or close
to three month transitional period during

00:00:10.759 --> 00:00:14.820
which Donald Trump is a very angry lame duck?

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.650
That's the first question today in audience
questions.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:22.640
David, what do you believe the transition
period would look like if Donald Trump loses?

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.429
So, first of all, I love the question and
I'm glad to explore it, but let's not get

00:00:27.429 --> 00:00:28.920
ahead of ourselves.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:34.280
We first need to vote and Joe Biden first
needs to win before we have to concern ourselves

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:37.469
with what a transition period would look like.

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:41.800
First of all, in the immediate, I would imagine,
a delayed concession.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:47.150
I think that if it is very, very close on
election night, Donald Trump will not concede.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:53.260
And if it is a blowout, Donald Trump may also
not concede under the guise that it's too

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.309
obviously fake.

00:00:55.309 --> 00:00:57.590
Trump couldn't possibly have lost by so much.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:00.860
So I think regardless of the results, there's
a good chance Trump does not concede.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.500
Now, just a reminder about concession.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.120
Concession is legally meaningless.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.220
Concession is a formality.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:12.150
It's done to show good faith, to signal the
beginning of a peaceful transition of power

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:15.090
and its norms and conventions and all that
different stuff.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:18.290
But the concession, legally speaking, is not
relevant.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:26.110
It is true, however, that if, for example,
a Republican concedes you may see Republican

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.540
secretaries of state who might get much more
involved in challenging results with recounts

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.920
or whatever, maybe not do it.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:39.850
So while legally not significant concessions
can still signal to governors and secretaries

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:44.360
of state around the country, how should you
react and what should you do next?

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:48.240
So Trump will in in all likelihood, it if
it's close.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.300
And it's likely to be close and Trump loses.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.150
Trump will likely say he was cheated or that
it was rigged.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.720
We only have to look at 2016.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:00.890
Remember, in 2016, Trump won and he still
to this day insists that the results were

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:05.660
false and that it was rigged against him because
losing the popular vote did not sufficient

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:09.149
sufficiently placate Donald Trump's massive
ego.

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:15.090
You will probably see a few Republicans who
would support Trump in claiming that it was

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.090
rigged.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:21.880
But my belief is that most Republicans are
going to largely accept the results.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:28.740
If indeed Joe Biden wins, then I wouldn't
be surprised if during the transition period

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.810
Trump doesn't invite Joe Biden to the White
House.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.810
This is a completely standard thing that's
done.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:35.620
The Bushes invited the Obamas, the Obamas
invited the Trumps.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:40.010
I wouldn't be shocked at all to see Donald
Trump break with that convention as well.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:45.230
But then what really matters about the transitional
period is going to be what does Donald Trump

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:50.380
try to do legislatively and via executive
order and in terms of judges and appointments

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.540
and nominations?

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:53.930
And what does he actually get done?

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:58.110
Because a lame duck trump that is furious
that he lost and believes it was rigged or

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:04.060
claims it was rigged is going to be even more
brazen and even more unscrupulous than we've

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.390
seen him be.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:10.490
I would expect a ton of executive orders,
some legal, some not legal.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:16.920
I would expect pardons that benefit him or
his interests in some direct or indirect way.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:22.660
And I would expect a scaling up of vicious,
vicious attacks against his political opponents.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:28.350
If Republicans controlled the House and by
the way, this is why this is so such an important

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:33.620
reason why the midterms mattered so much when
Democrats took the House.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:40.700
If Republicans controlled the House, you would
have the risk of a lame duck Trump doing Wisconsin

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:45.990
style legislation like when Scott Walker lost
the governorship in Wisconsin.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:51.620
Republicans in the legislature tried to weaken
the office of the governor for the incoming

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.150
Democrat to be able to do much less if Republicans
controlled the House.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.080
And Trump loses in November.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:03.670
You would likely see the same type of attempts
to limit the power of the office of the presidency.

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:07.540
It's not going to happen because Democrats
took the House in 2018.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:13.300
In terms of protests and aftermath, in terms
of aftermath, that would include protests

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.560
and unrest.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.579
I do think it depends on the margin of victory.

00:04:16.579 --> 00:04:22.820
I believe that a huge Biden victory would
set Trump off, but that it would really deflate

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.150
the sales of the Magga people.

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:30.900
A narrow victory by Biden will more credibly
let Trump claim it was rigged.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:38.060
And I would absolutely expect militia types,
patriot types, etc. to come out and protest.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.980
And there could be there could certainly be
violence and unrest.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:46.180
I do think that Mitch McConnell will keep
his eye on the ball and try to rapidly get

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:49.970
as many judges confirmed as possible during
a transition period for Trump.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:53.951
McConnell has been effective at doing this
legislation is unlikely again, because you

00:04:53.951 --> 00:04:59.700
need the House and the Democratically controlled
House is not going to give.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:05.389
Any big legislative concessions to a lame
duck Trump that they've just defeated, so

00:05:05.389 --> 00:05:08.630
I would expect a very messy November and December.

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:12.280
I would expect lawsuits, maybe recounts.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:17.020
And I don't think that they will actually
go anywhere if Joe Biden wins over that transition

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:18.020
period.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:23.100
Media will start to ignore Trump more and
more and focus on who is going to be in Biden's

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:30.320
cabinet, who from the from our allies are
coming back to the United States and saying,

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:31.320
we welcome you.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:33.450
We are glad that Trump is leaving.

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:36.500
And that will only further enrage Donald Trump
by missing anything.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:36.520
Let me know.

